{
  "id": "q-37265",
  "parts": [
    {
      "part": "problem",
      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "Which of the following sets is a subset of $A=\\{2n∣n\\in N\\}?$",
      "original_html_sha256": "07947f245023dd7c17ea9b8bb500191d001ae73c16f9813022bf8d832bff741a",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/07947f245023dd7c17ea9b8bb500191d001ae73c16f9813022bf8d832bff741a.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    },
    {
      "part": "worked_solution",
      "original_record": "history",
      "value": "First, we must find the elements of the set $A.$ The elements of the set \n$A$ are all the natural even numbers.\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\nA=\\{2,4,6,8,…\\}.\n$$\n\nNow, a subset of $A$ is a set whose elements are also elements of the set $A.$\n\nIn our case, $B=\\{2,6,12,14,32\\}$ is a subset of $A.$\n\nIn the rest of the options, the set $B$ has elements that are not in $A,$ meaning that it is not a subset of $A.$",
      "original_html_sha256": "12c22ca2be92a311c323045cb79f3d1ff2b6748ad5eaf662af889be5fcf92a46",
      "extractor_sha256": "1591183da328a4140792793d2cc113fd535ab5f25bc7f284ceb1b6f251efad18",
      "source_file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14071627/repairs/source-provenance-v2/structured-source/source/12c22ca2be92a311c323045cb79f3d1ff2b6748ad5eaf662af889be5fcf92a46.html",
      "extraction_errors": []
    }
  ]
}
